WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:03.550
Rita Linkner: "The Botox chemical
is physically addictive."

00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:06.840
I think Botox is like
getting your hair colored

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:07.770
or your nails done.

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:10.280
It's not like you have to,
but you're going to want to.

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:12.180
Jordana Herschthal: "Botox is so simple,

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:13.946
anyone can give an injection."

00:00:13.946 --> 00:00:15.850
My 2-year-old can push a plunger,

00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:19.100
but it's also very easy
to mess someone's face up.

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:22.060
"Botox will make you look emotionless."

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:23.830
Rita, can you tell I'm happy right now?

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:25.020
That's you happy?!

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:26.500
Hi, my name is Dr. Rita Linkner.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:29.810
I am a board-certified
dermatologist from New York City.

00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:33.490
I spend the majority of my day
doing injectables and lasers.

00:00:33.490 --> 00:00:35.450
Hi, I'm Dr. Jordana Herschthal,

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:37.380
and I'm a board-certified dermatologist

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:38.940
in Boca Raton, Florida,

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:42.050
and I love talking with patients
about their aesthetic goals

00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:44.410
and helping them see the full picture.

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:48.070
And we're here today to
debunk myths about Botox.

00:00:48.070 --> 00:00:50.170
Myths from social media.

00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:52.777
"Botox is toxic to your body."

00:00:52.777 --> 00:00:54.801
This is not true,

00:00:54.801 --> 00:00:57.834
but it's good to know
the history of Botox.

00:00:57.834 --> 00:00:59.610
Botox gets that name recognition.

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:02.470
It was the first neuromodulator
that was FDA approved,

00:01:02.470 --> 00:01:05.230
so it's a household name,
like Kleenex and Xerox.

00:01:05.230 --> 00:01:07.230
And so today we're going to be referring

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:09.550
to Botox as that umbrella term

00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:11.530
when we're discussing all
of the neuromodulators

00:01:11.530 --> 00:01:13.190
that are currently FDA approved.

00:01:13.190 --> 00:01:16.530
So, Botox contains a purified protein

00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:18.800
known as botulinum toxin,

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:23.010
which is derived from a
bacteria that causes botulism,

00:01:23.010 --> 00:01:24.780
which is toxic to your body.

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:29.510
However, Botox used appropriately
in appropriate dosing

00:01:29.510 --> 00:01:32.040
is very safe and very effective.

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:34.590
There are over 3,000 studies

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:37.181
proving its efficacy and safety.

00:01:37.181 --> 00:01:39.540
The other reason it is very safe to use

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:42.170
is we know that it stays
where we inject it.

00:01:42.170 --> 00:01:44.990
So it's not like you're
getting Botox in your forehead

00:01:44.990 --> 00:01:47.060
and it's going all over your body.

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:51.060
Botox is limited to where it is injected,

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:52.980
and it is safely metabolized

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:55.800
and excreted by your body in a few months.

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:58.300
I always tell patients
if Botox was dangerous,

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:00.060
I literally wouldn't have a pulse.

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:03.750
I'm someone who puts,
like, 100 units of Botox

00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:06.560
into my face and neck every
four and a half months.

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:08.800
And I have so for over a decade.

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:11.240
So, there are certain medical conditions

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:14.060
that are contraindicated
to the use of Botox.

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:16.280
So you should have a
very thorough discussion

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:19.800
with your provider before you
receive a Botox treatment.

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:21.740
"Botox is permanent."

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:23.160
So, let's debunk this one.

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:25.890
Botox is not permanent.

00:02:25.890 --> 00:02:29.470
Everybody metabolizes Botox differently.

00:02:29.470 --> 00:02:33.530
One of the great things about Botox is

00:02:33.530 --> 00:02:35.630
if you don't like the way it looks,

00:02:35.630 --> 00:02:39.470
it's completely out of your
system in three to six months.

00:02:39.470 --> 00:02:41.500
But it's also the worst thing,

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:43.150
because if you like the way it looks,

00:02:43.150 --> 00:02:44.490
you have to do it again.

00:02:44.490 --> 00:02:48.100
There is a super-Botox that's
out on the horizon, though,

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:50.400
that's looking to get FDA
approved later this year.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:53.470
It's going for FDA approval for
11s in between the eyebrows,

00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:56.430
and I can tell you
confidently that it works

00:02:56.430 --> 00:02:58.010
and it's going to have an indication

00:02:58.010 --> 00:03:00.750
that's going to be longer
than three to five months.

00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:04.130
Herschthal: "Some creams
and serums work like Botox."

00:03:04.130 --> 00:03:06.220
This is absolutely false.

00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:09.040
Botox works at the muscular level,

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:11.770
at specifically the
neuromuscular junction,

00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:14.460
to prevent the muscle from contracting.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:18.060
There is currently no
serum, cream, or facial

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:21.010
that can penetrate the skin deep enough

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:24.080
to exert action at the
level of the muscle.

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:27.880
And if it were true, it would
have to have FDA approval

00:03:27.880 --> 00:03:30.420
and it would not be
available over the counter.

00:03:30.420 --> 00:03:31.460
I completely agree.

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:32.990
I like to tell patients,

00:03:32.990 --> 00:03:34.480
you're genetically programmed

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:36.660
to move your muscles in a certain way,

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:39.950
and over time you get what
we call dynamic wrinkles,

00:03:39.950 --> 00:03:43.050
which are lines associated
with muscle movement.

00:03:43.050 --> 00:03:45.740
And the way Botox works
is it builds in resistance

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:48.660
so that you can't overutilize
those muscles anymore,

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:49.850
you can't crease them,

00:03:49.850 --> 00:03:52.330
and it basically helps
to smooth everything out.

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:55.973
So, next myth, "Getting
Botox is super painful."

00:03:56.880 --> 00:03:59.040
I would have to say this one's false.

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:02.270
The pain of a Botox
needle is pretty minimal,

00:04:02.270 --> 00:04:04.050
but it is similar to

00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:06.050
if you got, like, a
splinter in your finger

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:07.920
or perhaps a beesting.

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:10.740
Everybody's experience
with pain is different.

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:12.773
Linkner: They're insulin needles.

00:04:12.773 --> 00:04:14.881
They're as small as you can get.

00:04:14.881 --> 00:04:17.330
And it goes faster than
people think, also.

00:04:17.330 --> 00:04:18.708
Though I think location on the face

00:04:18.708 --> 00:04:21.390
does make a big difference
in terms of sensitivity.

00:04:21.390 --> 00:04:24.150
And this relates to how important it is

00:04:24.150 --> 00:04:26.373
for your provider to really have

00:04:26.373 --> 00:04:28.618
a deep understanding of anatomy

00:04:28.618 --> 00:04:31.690
when you're getting any sort
of injectable on your face.

00:04:31.690 --> 00:04:34.760
I mean, I can do a full
face, a full neck of Botox

00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:36.550
in probably under four minutes.

00:04:36.550 --> 00:04:38.750
And if people are really
averse to needles,

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:40.420
you could always topically numb someone

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:41.870
to help that pain dissipate.

00:04:41.870 --> 00:04:43.390
There are other little tricks,

00:04:43.390 --> 00:04:46.820
like vibration devices and also ice.

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:49.460
And even for patients
who are really sensitive,

00:04:49.460 --> 00:04:50.810
we break out the Pro-Nox,

00:04:50.810 --> 00:04:52.560
which is half-dose laughing gas,

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:55.790
and that always calms
patients down immediately

00:04:55.790 --> 00:04:57.800
and leaves your system
within five minutes.

00:04:57.800 --> 00:05:01.290
Linkner: "The Botox chemical
is physically addictive."

00:05:01.290 --> 00:05:04.522
I think Botox is like
getting your hair colored

00:05:04.522 --> 00:05:05.550
or your nails done.

00:05:05.550 --> 00:05:07.170
This is how I like to
explain it to patients

00:05:07.170 --> 00:05:08.940
who ask me, "If I do this once,

00:05:08.940 --> 00:05:10.470
do I have to keep doing this
for the rest of my life?"

00:05:10.470 --> 00:05:13.000
It's not like you have to,
but you're going to want to.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:15.510
So, I always liken aesthetic treatments

00:05:15.510 --> 00:05:17.710
like Botox, fillers, and lasers

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:20.780
to maintaining any organ in your system.

00:05:20.780 --> 00:05:23.730
You get your teeth cleaned
two to four times a year

00:05:23.730 --> 00:05:24.840
or whatever it is;

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:26.750
you get your aesthetic treatments

00:05:26.750 --> 00:05:28.710
because you're always aging.

00:05:28.710 --> 00:05:31.960
These treatments do not
stop the aging process,

00:05:31.960 --> 00:05:34.890
but these treatments will help you age

00:05:34.890 --> 00:05:36.830
the way you want to age.

00:05:36.830 --> 00:05:39.730
Linkner: Myth experts hear the most.

00:05:39.730 --> 00:05:43.580
"Botox is so simple, anyone
can give an injection."

00:05:43.580 --> 00:05:48.010
On the one hand, giving
an injection is very easy.

00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:50.420
Anyone can push a plunger,

00:05:50.420 --> 00:05:52.410
my 2-year-old can push a plunger,

00:05:52.410 --> 00:05:55.520
but it's also very easy
to mess someone's face up.

00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:57.080
So it's really critical

00:05:57.080 --> 00:06:00.850
that your provider has a
deep understanding of anatomy

00:06:00.850 --> 00:06:04.230
and how these medicines affect anatomy

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:07.463
to give you reproducible,

00:06:07.463 --> 00:06:09.813
great aesthetic outcomes.

00:06:09.813 --> 00:06:12.690
So, Jordana and I are
board-certified dermatologists.

00:06:12.690 --> 00:06:14.890
It took each of us over a decade

00:06:14.890 --> 00:06:16.440
to get to the point where we were able

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:18.408
to put a syringe in our hands

00:06:18.408 --> 00:06:20.808
and utilize the medicine in it

00:06:20.808 --> 00:06:23.020
to create facial aesthetics.

00:06:23.020 --> 00:06:25.180
Both Jordana and I, still to this day,

00:06:25.180 --> 00:06:28.070
we take courses religiously
where we're learning

00:06:28.070 --> 00:06:30.150
from the best international patients

00:06:30.150 --> 00:06:31.920
and doing dissection courses.

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:33.800
And we're still reading every day

00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:35.310
to really be the best teachers

00:06:35.310 --> 00:06:37.320
that we can be for our patients.

00:06:37.320 --> 00:06:39.760
"Botox and fillers are the same."

00:06:39.760 --> 00:06:41.360
I love this myth,

00:06:41.360 --> 00:06:45.880
because I probably address
it at least once a day.

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:48.638
Almost every line on your face

00:06:48.638 --> 00:06:51.063
can be addressed with filler,

00:06:51.063 --> 00:06:54.170
but not every line can
be addressed with Botox.

00:06:54.170 --> 00:06:57.330
Botox works at the level of the muscle

00:06:57.330 --> 00:07:00.280
to relax muscles of contraction.

00:07:00.280 --> 00:07:03.670
It is preventing and
diminishing those static lines,

00:07:03.670 --> 00:07:05.260
or lines at rest.

00:07:05.260 --> 00:07:09.290
Fillers, on the other hand,
are used to address volume loss

00:07:09.290 --> 00:07:11.630
that occurs in our face as we age.

00:07:11.630 --> 00:07:15.050
So, we all have fat
compartments all over our face.

00:07:15.050 --> 00:07:18.550
And as we age, they deflate
and descend with time,

00:07:18.550 --> 00:07:22.890
so we use fillers to
restore that lost volume

00:07:22.890 --> 00:07:25.880
and give a more youthful
shape to the face.

00:07:25.880 --> 00:07:29.590
"Botox injections need
a lot of recovery time."

00:07:29.590 --> 00:07:33.380
The only issue with Botox
is if you get a bruise,

00:07:33.380 --> 00:07:35.050
but there really isn't downtime.

00:07:35.050 --> 00:07:37.150
There's about an hour after the procedure

00:07:37.150 --> 00:07:40.590
where you will see little
bumps under the skin,

00:07:40.590 --> 00:07:43.110
and that's the solution of the Botox

00:07:43.110 --> 00:07:44.800
that was placed under the skin.

00:07:44.800 --> 00:07:46.960
You are taking a needle and
putting it into your skin,

00:07:46.960 --> 00:07:48.590
so you just want to make sure that you're

00:07:48.590 --> 00:07:50.440
not doing anything to
really thin your blood,

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:52.610
which would increase the
chances of getting a bruise.

00:07:52.610 --> 00:07:55.860
So ideally not drinking
alcohol the night before

00:07:55.860 --> 00:07:58.300
or even caffeine the
morning of really helps.

00:07:58.300 --> 00:08:00.890
If you have really high
tendency towards bruising,

00:08:00.890 --> 00:08:02.610
it's nice to take oral arnica.

00:08:02.610 --> 00:08:04.750
I can always tell when
I'm injecting a patient.

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:06.260
I call it the booze ooze.

00:08:06.260 --> 00:08:09.150
It's like this slow ooze after you inject,

00:08:09.150 --> 00:08:11.660
and I know that they've
had a glass of wine

00:08:11.660 --> 00:08:13.950
or a martini the night before.

00:08:13.950 --> 00:08:16.530
Linkner: My only rule that I have

00:08:16.530 --> 00:08:18.720
for my patients when Botox goes in

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:20.690
is no exercising for six hours.

00:08:20.690 --> 00:08:23.140
Herschthal: My only rule
is don't touch the Botox,

00:08:23.140 --> 00:08:26.100
because I don't want you
spreading it to a different area

00:08:26.100 --> 00:08:28.410
in the forehead or the glabella area,

00:08:28.410 --> 00:08:30.810
because you could get into trouble

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:33.010
with dropping somebody's lid.

00:08:33.010 --> 00:08:37.950
So, the muscles that keep
the brow elevated will drop,

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:41.240
and then the patient will
appear to have a heavier lid.

00:08:41.240 --> 00:08:43.720
Again, these are not
permanent side effects,

00:08:43.720 --> 00:08:46.270
but they are undesirable side effects.

00:08:46.270 --> 00:08:49.270
"Botox accumulates in the body."

00:08:49.270 --> 00:08:51.020
I wish that was true,

00:08:51.020 --> 00:08:53.303
but unfortunately it does not.

00:08:53.303 --> 00:08:55.430
Every week that your Botox is in,

00:08:55.430 --> 00:08:57.840
it incrementally decreases.

00:08:57.840 --> 00:08:59.880
It's not like it just turns off overnight.

00:08:59.880 --> 00:09:01.960
I will tell you, in this pandemic,

00:09:01.960 --> 00:09:04.030
I'm noticing people are exercising more,

00:09:04.030 --> 00:09:05.790
and that's making their Botox metabolize

00:09:05.790 --> 00:09:06.970
a little bit faster.

00:09:06.970 --> 00:09:08.200
So I get that question a lot.

00:09:08.200 --> 00:09:10.320
You know, "How do we make
my Botox last longer?"

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:11.880
And it is dose dependent.

00:09:11.880 --> 00:09:14.810
So if you put more in, it
might not look so natural

00:09:14.810 --> 00:09:15.870
for those first few weeks,

00:09:15.870 --> 00:09:19.301
but it should get you to
last a couple of weeks longer

00:09:19.301 --> 00:09:21.210
than when you were using a lower dose.

00:09:21.210 --> 00:09:23.240
Herschthal: Myths from pop culture.

00:09:23.240 --> 00:09:26.300
"Botox will make you look emotionless."

00:09:26.300 --> 00:09:29.110
I'm hearing the hate, but
I'm not seeing the hate.

00:09:29.110 --> 00:09:30.720
Rita, can you tell I'm happy right now?

00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:32.180
That's you happy?!

00:09:32.180 --> 00:09:36.040
So, I think "emotionless" is
a little bit of a strong word

00:09:36.040 --> 00:09:39.170
to describe the effects of Botox.

00:09:39.170 --> 00:09:42.620
If you have an open
conversation with your provider

00:09:42.620 --> 00:09:46.750
about what your desires are
for your Botox treatment,

00:09:46.750 --> 00:09:49.830
you can easily get a treatment

00:09:49.830 --> 00:09:51.180
that is more natural looking

00:09:51.180 --> 00:09:54.550
where you still preserve some
movement in the upper face.

00:09:54.550 --> 00:09:56.327
It's been exactly eight days

00:09:56.327 --> 00:09:58.030
since Jordana put my Botox in.

00:09:58.030 --> 00:09:59.470
It hasn't peaked out yet,

00:09:59.470 --> 00:10:02.510
but it's starting to get
tighter on me every single day.

00:10:02.510 --> 00:10:03.880
Do I love how it looks?

00:10:03.880 --> 00:10:04.840
I mean, I do.

00:10:04.840 --> 00:10:07.300
Do I love how my children
can't tell what I'm thinking?

00:10:07.300 --> 00:10:08.200
I love that.

00:10:08.200 --> 00:10:09.490
So you really have to figure out

00:10:09.490 --> 00:10:11.800
where you want to run on that spectrum.

00:10:11.800 --> 00:10:14.520
Herschthal: "Botox is
only used cosmetically."

00:10:14.520 --> 00:10:17.812
So, Botox was actually first FDA approved

00:10:17.812 --> 00:10:19.745
in 1989.

00:10:19.745 --> 00:10:21.120
And that was for the use

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:24.560
of two medical disorders of the eye,

00:10:24.560 --> 00:10:28.320
which is called strabismus
and blepharospasm.

00:10:28.320 --> 00:10:31.000
It wasn't actually until 2002

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:33.670
that Botox got its first FDA approval

00:10:33.670 --> 00:10:35.220
for cosmetic indication.

00:10:35.220 --> 00:10:36.350
Well, thank goodness

00:10:36.350 --> 00:10:38.550
those oculoplastic surgeons were trying

00:10:38.550 --> 00:10:41.290
to treat these overexercising eye muscles,

00:10:41.290 --> 00:10:42.960
because that's when they saw

00:10:42.960 --> 00:10:46.290
that the 11s in between the
eyebrows were disappearing.

00:10:46.290 --> 00:10:47.880
So it's because of strabismus

00:10:47.880 --> 00:10:51.400
that all of us don't have
lines on our face anymore.

00:10:51.400 --> 00:10:53.930
So, Botox has actually been around

00:10:53.930 --> 00:10:55.380
for over 30 years,

00:10:55.380 --> 00:10:58.100
and it has over 27 indications,

00:10:58.100 --> 00:11:00.470
most of which are medical.

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:03.710
Linkner: A very common
use is for oversweating.

00:11:03.710 --> 00:11:06.780
So in the underarms,
hands, and feet are places,

00:11:06.780 --> 00:11:09.370
because Botox does
attack that little muscle

00:11:09.370 --> 00:11:11.640
on every sweat gland
that helps you to sweat.

00:11:11.640 --> 00:11:14.180
It can turn that off so that
you can decrease sweating.

00:11:14.180 --> 00:11:16.810
I've also used it medically for migraines.

00:11:16.810 --> 00:11:20.826
The list of FDA indications
for medical Botox

00:11:20.826 --> 00:11:22.734
is so long.

00:11:22.734 --> 00:11:25.430
"Only older women get Botox."

00:11:25.430 --> 00:11:27.990
Ugh! No, that's so false.

00:11:27.990 --> 00:11:30.310
I was 27 the first time

00:11:30.310 --> 00:11:32.510
that I put Botox into my crow's-feet.

00:11:32.510 --> 00:11:36.270
And I will tell you, it's
something that I do religiously

00:11:36.270 --> 00:11:38.550
and have done every four and a half months

00:11:38.550 --> 00:11:40.430
for the past decade.

00:11:40.430 --> 00:11:42.550
So, I like to say that Botox

00:11:42.550 --> 00:11:46.270
is not gender nor is it age specific.

00:11:46.270 --> 00:11:48.300
There's also a huge increase

00:11:48.300 --> 00:11:50.330
in male patients coming in,

00:11:50.330 --> 00:11:52.130
specifically for their crow's-feet.

00:11:52.130 --> 00:11:56.121
People are wanting to look their best,

00:11:56.121 --> 00:11:57.262
feel their best.

00:11:57.262 --> 00:12:02.020
So Botox is not age and
it is not gender specific.

00:12:02.020 --> 00:12:04.530
Linkner: "Botox works right away."

00:12:04.530 --> 00:12:07.300
[sighs] It's the Botox.

00:12:07.300 --> 00:12:09.900
I can't show emotion for
another hour and a half.

00:12:09.900 --> 00:12:13.250
So, truthfully, Botox can take,

00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:14.960
it takes a couple of days to kick in.

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:18.180
So let's say your Botox goes in Friday;

00:12:18.180 --> 00:12:20.240
you're not going to start
to really feel those results

00:12:20.240 --> 00:12:22.160
into Sunday, into Monday.

00:12:22.160 --> 00:12:24.930
It takes a full two weeks to peak out.

00:12:24.930 --> 00:12:26.738
And at that two-week period,

00:12:26.738 --> 00:12:28.446
incrementally every single week

00:12:28.446 --> 00:12:30.790
you'll gain a little bit of movement back.

00:12:30.790 --> 00:12:33.397
Everybody metabolizes
this stuff differently.

00:12:33.397 --> 00:12:35.261
I think we look natural.

00:12:35.261 --> 00:12:39.280
I think we're doing a good
job of looking natural.

00:12:39.280 --> 00:12:41.310
We have code words with each other.

00:12:41.310 --> 00:12:43.440
So if, like, Jordana
tells me the code word,

00:12:43.440 --> 00:12:46.520
then I know I've gone to over the line.

00:12:46.520 --> 00:12:48.283
Yeah, we've gone over the edge.

